          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+field"} ordered field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is
            %strong real closed
            if it satisfies the following two properties:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Any non-negative element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \geq 0
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+root"} square root
                in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %li
              %p
                Any odd-degree
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
                with coefficients in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                has a root in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            Notice that the order on a real closed field is definable from the algebraic structure:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
            if and only if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi z
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists_z x + z^2 = y
            %em unique
            ordering on a real closed field, defined by taking the positive elements to be precisely the nonzero squares.) In fact, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of real closed fields and order-preserving field homomorphisms is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Field"} Field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
            and field homomorphisms.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p Real closed fields can be equivalently characterized by any of the following properties:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is not
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+extension"} extension
                is. This extension is necessarily
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msqrt
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F[\sqrt{-1}]
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+algebra"} fundamental theorem of algebra
            %li
              %p
                As a field,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+equivalence"} elementarily equivalent
                to the field of real numbers.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intermediate+value+theorem"} intermediate value theorem
                holds for all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+functions"} polynomial functions
                with coefficients in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is an ordered field that has no ordered algebraic extension.
          %p
            In fact, there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion"} completion
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+field"} ordered field
            to a real closed field, in the following sense:
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p The full inclusion of the category of real closed fields and field homomorphisms to the category of ordered fields and ordered field homomorphisms has a left adjoint.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We give a brief sketch of proof, referring to Lang’s
              %em Algebra
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 3
                      %mi rd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3^{rd}
              edition), section IX.2, for more details.
            %p
              First, for each ordered field
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to R
              that is order-preserving (theorem 2.11). This is called a
              %strong real closure
              of the ordered field
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %p
              Second, any two real closures of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              are uniquely isomorphic (theorem 2.9); in fact, the proof shows there is at most one order-preserving homomorphism over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              between any two real closures. Therefore we may speak of
              %em the
              real closure of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi F
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widebar{F}
            %p
              Finally, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to R
              be any order-preserving field homomorphism to a real closed field
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to R
              extends uniquely to a homomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mover
                        %mi F
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: \widebar{F} \to R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              must factor through the subfield
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R' \hookrightarrow R
              consisting of elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in R
              that are algebraic over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widebar{F}
              is algebraic over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widebar{F} \to R'
              extending
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to R'
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            %li
              %p
                Real
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number"} algebraic number
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            %li
              %p
                A field of nonstandard real numbers (as in Robinson
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonstandard+analysis"} nonstandard analysis
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surreal+number"} Surreal numbers
                form a (large) real closed field.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is real closed, then the field of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Puiseux+series"} Puiseux series
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is also real closed.
            %li
              %p
                More generally, given a real closed field
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hahn+series"} Hahn series
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valuation+ring"} value group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                (a linearly ordered group) is real closed provided that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/divisible+group"} divisible
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/o-minimal+structure"} o-minimal
                ordered ring structure
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a real closed field.
            %li
              %p
                Given an o-minimal ordered ring
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/germ"} germ
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to R
                in any o-minimal expansion of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo ,
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R, 0, 1, +, -, \cdot, \lt)
                is real closed. (By “germ at infinity”, we mean an equivalence class of functions for which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \equiv g
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = g(x)
                for all sufficiently large
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          %h2#infinites_and_infinitesimals Infinites and infinitesimals
          %p
            Each real closed field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            contains a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valuation+ring"} valuation
            subring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \hookrightarrow R
            consisting of the “bounded” or archimedean elements, i.e., elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in R
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -n \leq x \leq n
            for some integer multiple
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            of the identity. An element in the complement of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is an
            %strong infinite
            element of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %strong infinitesimal
            element. The field of fractions of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is clearly
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            We remark that any real closed field contains a copy of the field of real
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+numbers"} algebraic numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widebar{\mathbb{Q}}
            (not to be confused with the algebraic closure of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widebar{\mathbb{Q}}
            is archimedean.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^\ast
            be the group of units of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^\ast/B^\ast
            is the
            %strong value group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is real closed, then the value group is a linearly ordered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/divisible+group"} divisible group
            (divisible because we can take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi n
                    %mi th
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n^{th}
            roots of positive elements in
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            In the other direction, to each ordered divisible abelian group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            as its value group. For example, one may form the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hahn+series"} Hahn series
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widebar{\mathbb{Q}}
            with value group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h2#in_constructive_mathematics In constructive mathematics
          %p
            In constructive mathematics, the various definitions of real closed field bifurcate, because of different definitions of an odd-degree polynomial. One could define an odd-degree polynomial as a polynomial whose coefficient for an odd number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/denial+inequality"} not equal to
            zero and whose coefficient for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \gt n
            for is equal to zero. On the other hand, one could also define an odd-degree polynomial as a polynomial whose coefficient for an odd number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+apartness+relation"} apart from
            zero and whose coefficient for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \gt n
            for is equal to zero. These two definitions are different from each other, the real numbers satisfy the second, while they do not satisfy the first.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "Euclidean+geometry#TarskiAxioms"} Euclidean geometry – Tarski’s axioms
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serge+Lang"}> Serge Lang
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebra
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4613-0041-0"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4613-0041-0
            %li
              %p
                David Marker,
                %em Notes on Real Algebra
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uic.edu/~marker/orsay/real_algebra.pdf"} (link)
